0|0@MensRights^1439968756#cu8102h:chocoboat$:&gt; I don't understand what's troubling about it. I don't think sex as a commodity is a good thing for society. I'm far from a "family values" conservative here, but I still think that long term relationships are good for society, especially when children are involved. Not that they would never exist with legal prostitution, but I think the rates of long term relationships would drop significantly over time. I also don't like the idea that a vagina is inherently valuable, and that mindset leads people to think that women are more valuable than men. And more than ever, women in a relationship would be thinking "I'm giving him his valuable vagina-access, he owes me for it, he better give me something valuable." I understand the arguments in favor of it though. A safe and well-regulated industry would be great for sex workers, and "you pay for it one way or another" is a common sentiment among some men. I don't know though, I just feel like it would do more harm than good. I consider myself a very progressive person, but even this is too much for me. It's hard to imagine legalized prostitution getting much public support. 
